index 0000000..51f0031
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ANSWER.md
@@ -0,0 +1,64 @@
+# Why the nightly review never reported anything
+
+The evidence is in `Library/Logs/nightly-review.err`. It holds 6 identical pairs of lines, matching
+`runs = 6` / `last exit code = 1` in `launchctl-print.txt`. So launchd **is** running the job
+every night. The job just fails before it can tell you.
+
+## Cause 1: the failure path itself crashes (why you never got a failure note)
+
+```
+/Users/vk/bin/nightly-review.zsh:19: read-only variable: status
+```
+
+The script runs under `/bin/zsh`, and in zsh `status` is a read-only special
+parameter (an alias of `$?`). The line `status=$?` is a fatal error, so the script exits
+with code 1 right there, before either `notify.sh` call. Success and failure both end
+the same way: silently. (This would work in bash, which is probably why it looked fine.)
+
+**Fix:** use `rc=$?` instead (`bin/nightly-review.zsh`).
+
+## Cause 2: `claude` isn't authenticated under launchd (why the review fails)
+
+```
+Not logged in · Please run /login
+```
+
+launchd doesn't start a login shell and never reads `~/.zshrc`/`~/.zprofile`. Its
+environment has only the plist's `PATH` (see `environment = {...}` in the
+launchctl output). Whatever authenticates `claude` in your terminal (for example an exported
+`ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`/token in your shell profile) isn't there, so `claude -p` exits
+non-zero immediately. You can't see that because of Cause 1.
+
+**Fix:** the script now loads a long-lived token from the keychain when none is in the
+environment, the same way `notify.sh` gets the Telegram token. If the token is missing, it sends a clear
+failure note. One-time setup on your Mac:
+
+```sh
+claude setup-token          # prints a long-lived OAuth token
+security add-generic-password -s claude-nightly-token -a "$USER" -w '<token>'
+```
+
+## Problems that would have bitten next (also fixed)
+
+3. **Headless `claude -p` can't approve tool use.** The prompt needs `git log`/`git show`,
+   but in `-p` mode nobody is there to approve a Bash call, so it gets denied and the
+   "review" would see no commits. Read-only tools are now pre-approved with
+   `--allowedTools "Read" "Grep" "Glob" "Bash(git log:*)" "Bash(git show:*)" "Bash(git diff:*)"`.
+   Nothing that can write is allowed, so "Do not modify any file" is enforced, not just
+   requested.
+4. **Telegram errors were swallowed.** `curl -sS` without `--fail` exits 0 on HTTP
+   400/401, and the response was sent to `/dev/null`. A bad token or a rejected message
+   would look like success. `notify.sh` now uses `--fail-with-body` and prints Telegram's
+   error to stderr, which lands in `nightly-review.err` under launchd.
+5. **The summary could be cut mid-character.** `head -c 300` cuts at byte 300, which can split a
+   multi-byte UTF-8 character, and Telegram rejects invalid UTF-8. The script now sets
+   a UTF-8 locale (launchd sets none) and cuts at 300 *characters* with
+   `${summary[1,300]}`.
+6. Every `notify` call in the script now logs to stderr if `notify.sh` fails, so a broken
+   notifier also leaves a trace in `nightly-review.err`.
+
+## After deploying
+
+Copy `bin/*` back to `~/bin`. The plist didn't need changes, so no reload is required.
+To test without waiting for 02:30, run `launchctl kickstart gui/$UID/com.vk.nightly-review`,
+then check Telegram and `~/Library/Logs/nightly-review.err`.
diff --git a/bin/nightly-review.zsh b/bin/nightly-review.zsh
index e0b986f..6075e52 100755
--- a/bin/nightly-review.zsh
+++ b/bin/nightly-review.zsh
@@ -2,10 +2,29 @@
 # Nightly review of yesterday's commits, summary to Telegram.
 set -u
 
+# launchd gives us no locale; needed so the summary is truncated on
+# character (not byte) boundaries and stays valid UTF-8 for Telegram.
+export LANG=en_US.UTF-8 LC_ALL=en_US.UTF-8
+
 REPO="$HOME/projects/shop"
 OUT="$HOME/Library/Logs/nightly-review-$(date +%F).md"
 NOTIFY="$HOME/bin/notify.sh"
 
+notify() {
+  "$NOTIFY" "$1" || print -u2 "nightly review: notify.sh failed (exit $?)"
+}
+
+# launchd does not read ~/.zshrc, so claude has no credentials here.
+# Long-lived token from `claude setup-token`, stored once with:
+#   security add-generic-password -s claude-nightly-token -a "$USER" -w '<token>'
+if [[ -z "${CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN:-}" && -z "${ANTHROPIC_API_KEY:-}" ]]; then
+  CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=$(security find-generic-password -s claude-nightly-token -w 2>/dev/null) || {
+    notify "nightly review FAILED: no Claude token in keychain (claude-nightly-token)"
+    exit 1
+  }
+  export CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN
+fi
+
 SINCE=$(date -v-1d +%F)
 PROMPT="Review the commits in this repository since $SINCE.
 For each commit: one line on what it changes and whether anything looks risky
@@ -13,14 +32,19 @@ For each commit: one line on what it changes and whether anything looks risky
 End with a three-line summary I can read on my phone.
 Do not modify any file."
 
-cd "$REPO" || { "$NOTIFY" "nightly review: repo missing"; exit 1; }
+cd "$REPO" || { notify "nightly review: repo missing"; exit 1; }
 
-claude -p "$PROMPT" --output-format text > "$OUT"
-status=$?
+# Headless mode can't ask for permission: pre-approve read-only tools only,
+# otherwise every `git log` is denied and the review sees nothing.
+claude -p "$PROMPT" --output-format text \
+  --allowedTools "Read" "Grep" "Glob" "Bash(git log:*)" "Bash(git show:*)" "Bash(git diff:*)" \
+  > "$OUT"
+rc=$?   # `status` is a read-only special parameter in zsh
 
-if [ $status -ne 0 ]; then
-  "$NOTIFY" "nightly review FAILED (exit $status), see $OUT"
-  exit $status
+if (( rc != 0 )); then
+  notify "nightly review FAILED (exit $rc), see $OUT and ~/Library/Logs/nightly-review.err"
+  exit $rc
 fi
 
-"$NOTIFY" "nightly review done: $(head -c 300 "$OUT")"
+summary=$(<"$OUT")
+notify "nightly review done: ${summary[1,300]}"
diff --git a/bin/notify.sh b/bin/notify.sh
index 818e531..d4c7237 100755
--- a/bin/notify.sh
+++ b/bin/notify.sh
@@ -3,5 +3,7 @@
 set -eu
 : "${TG_BOT_TOKEN:=$(security find-generic-password -s tg-bot -w)}"
 CHAT_ID=123456789
-curl -sS -X POST "https://api.telegram.org/bot${TG_BOT_TOKEN}/sendMessage" \
-  -d chat_id="$CHAT_ID" --data-urlencode text="$1" > /dev/null
+# --fail-with-body: Telegram API errors (bad token, bad text) become a non-zero
+# exit, and the reason goes to stderr instead of /dev/null.
+resp=$(curl -sS --fail-with-body -X POST "https://api.telegram.org/bot${TG_BOT_TOKEN}/sendMessage" \
+  -d chat_id="$CHAT_ID" --data-urlencode text="$1") || { echo "notify.sh: $resp" >&2; exit 1; }
